module std where

-- or — short-circuit logical OR. (Boolean, Boolean) → Boolean.
--
-- The clause LHS is the bare `or` (id `std:or`). Phase 5b6's `orFn` divergence +
-- the std.ts `f.id === "std-or:orFn"` extraction seam are RETIRED by the
-- word-operator de-reservation precursor (`5121c5b8`, ahead of FM-retire-9 9a),
-- which made `and`/`or`/`not` ordinary idents. No `@codeName`.
--
-- Pure expression; mirrors the pre-Phase-5b6 inline JSON-Logic body
-- at engine/src/modules/std.ts:2396 (`{or: [{var: "a"}, {var: "b"}]}`),
-- which dispatched via the named-op key `or` to `applyOp`'s short-
-- circuit case branch in json-logic.ts.
--
-- Decomposed via if-lowering: `if a then True else b`. The post-flip
-- body lowers to `{if: [{var: "a"}, {construct: ["True"]}, {var: "b"}]}`
-- — canonical structural-form dispatch through `applyOp`'s `if` branch,
-- which evaluates ONLY the chosen branch. Lazy-semantics preserved:
-- `b` is only evaluated when `a` is false (mirror of `and`'s laziness
-- with branches swapped).
--
-- If-lowering source-of-truth migration (5b5 piloted on min/max; 5b6 extended to
-- Boolean short-circuits). Disproves the 5b5 "lazy-arg semantics blocker" framing
-- — short-circuit forms ARE portable via if-lowering through `applyOp`'s
-- structural-form case branch.

@label "Or"
@description "Logical OR — true when either operand is truthy. Short-circuit via if-lowering (Phase 5b6): `b` is only evaluated when `a` is false."
@tags "boolean" "operator"
or : (a: Boolean) -> (b: Boolean) -> Boolean
or a b = if a then True else b
